            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical observation on O3 acupoint injection for treatment of low back pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>115-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To explore the value of O3 acupoint injection for treatment of low back pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">One hundred and twenty cases of low back pain were randomly divided into an electroacupuncture (EA) group, a Danggui injectio point injection group and an O3 acupoint injection group. They were treated with EA, Danggui acupoint injection and O3 (30 microg/mL) acupoint injection at Qihaishu (BL 24), Dachangshu (BL 25), Guanyuanshu (BL 25) and local Ashi points.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">There were significant differences in the therapeutic effect as the O3 acupoint injection group compared with the EA group and the Danggui point injection group (P &lt; 0.01 or P &lt; 0.05), but there was no significant difference between the EA group and the Danggui point injection group (P &gt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The O3 acupoint injection is a convenient and highly effective therapy for low back pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
